# CRITICAL TERMINAL COMMAND LENGTH RULE
- NEVER run 
ode -e or pass multi-line scripts/code inside a terminal command.
- Long terminal commands crash the Antigravity UI confirmation button.
- Every terminal command MUST be a single short line under 80 characters (e.g., 
ode test_script.mjs or 
pm test).
- When you need to run custom test code or API checks, ALWAYS use the file creation tool to write a temporary .mjs file first, run 
ode temp_check.mjs, and delete it afterward.
